WEBVTT

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:21.520
In a place far removed from here,
the cherry blossoms were in bloom.

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:26.020
We had made up our minds that
we were going to go see them.

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:28.270
The cherry blossoms aren't going away.

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:32.360
In fact, they would be
approaching here as time passed.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:37.160
That was why we couldn't dawdle.

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:42.370
A time of joy that could only come during
the winter was becoming that much shorter.

00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:49.290
Less than two days had passed
since we came up with our plan,

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:52.210
and we were finished
getting ready for our trip.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:57.550
We packed the minimum amount
that we could fit into my Cub.

00:00:57.550 --> 00:01:01.180
We would lodge at business
hotels and net cafés.

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:11.570
I'm off.

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:18.570
Our route was still undecided.

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:23.080
Our destination was the farthest place
from us where they were in bloom.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:32.340
Thanks for waiting.

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:35.920
We leave on our journey today...

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.680
...to go and seize spring.

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:17.530
Girls.

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:21.570
Please take this with you.

00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:24.910
<i>Komisbrot</i>--the rye bread of soldiers.

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:25.950
Oh...!

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:27.790
It will keep longer than normal bread.

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:30.210
Hooray! Thank you very much!

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:31.040
Not at all.

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:32.620
Mama...

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:36.500
If anything happens, Koguma-<i>san</i>
will keep me safe, so I'll be fine.

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:40.130
And if anything happens to me,
Shii-<i>chan </i>will keep me safe.

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:43.930
My Super Cub will keep me safe.

00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:46.640
Mm-hmm. No matter what
happens, we'll be fine.

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:48.430
We'll have the Super Cub along with us.

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:51.980
My Hunter Cub is even stronger!

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:53.440
Well...

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:57.110
...it's getting to be that time.

00:04:07.990 --> 00:04:10.080
Come back safely.

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:12.120
Be careful, okay?

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:15.750
Okay.

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:22.010
Off we go!

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:42.110
If we turn right and head south
from Nirasaki along the Fuji River,

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:44.450
we should reach Shizuoka
in about three hours.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.160
If we keep on heading along the coast,

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:49.240
we could see cherry blossoms along
the Pacific coast before the day is out.

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:50.290
That won't do.

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:52.910
Of course not. That wouldn't be any fun.

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:56.710
We're going as far away as
we can to capture spring.

00:04:56.710 --> 00:04:58.170
Right.

00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:53.350
We're taking a break already?
We've only been at it for an hour.

00:05:53.350 --> 00:05:55.560
Whenever going on a long-distance trip,

00:05:55.560 --> 00:05:59.940
any signs of trouble that could later
lead to critical system failure

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:02.150
will come to your attention
within the first hour.

00:06:02.150 --> 00:06:04.070
It's the devil's 60 minutes.

00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:09.030
Which is why, after riding for an hour,
we stop and re-inspect each part.

00:06:09.030 --> 00:06:12.330
If we can ride through this
first hour without a hitch,

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:14.660
then the following dozens,
or even hundreds of hours,

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:17.040
will most commonly
come off with no trouble.

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:20.330
See, it's sort of a superstition
among bikers.

00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:22.880
Is that right?

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:28.380
This is the first time I've ever gone down
the Koshu Highway to its end.

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:36.060
The road keeps going. Now we have to
decide which road we're going to take.

00:06:37.270 --> 00:06:40.480
We keep on this route until
the junction at Shiojiri.

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:44.440
Then hop on National Route 19.
We pass through the mountains in Kiso,

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:48.650
then follow the Chuo Main Line down.
It's the shortest route to Nagoya.

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:51.950
We have to at least get past
Nagoya today, don't we?

00:06:51.950 --> 00:06:54.620
Yes. And by following the tracks,

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:56.540
it's easier to handle anything
that might come up.

00:06:56.540 --> 00:06:58.250
I'd like to go up to the Sea of Japan

00:06:58.250 --> 00:07:01.250
and ride through the sea spray
of the surging waves along there.

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:03.130
It's hard to consider that safe.

00:07:03.130 --> 00:07:05.340
Besides, there's no way
the salt air will be good

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:08.720
for the pressed steel frames on our Cubs.

00:07:12.890 --> 00:07:17.100
Uh, I have to agree with
Koguma-<i>san</i>'s decision.

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:19.600
I see. Okay, then that's what we'll do.

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:21.850
Huh? Are you sure?

00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:30.200
I can ride down any road
I want to whenever I like.

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:12.430
Matsunoyasabo Coffee 

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:16.370
The Nakasendo was one of the five routes
that flourished during the Edo period.

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:18.160
It had a lot of rest areas.

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:19.410
Oh, yeah?

00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:22.500
There are lots of old teahouses
left over from that time, too.

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:26.000
If you're going to run a café,
it couldn't hurt to have a look at them.

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:29.760
That explains it. So this is why
we're taking the Kiso route.

00:08:53.150 --> 00:08:54.950
Lunchtime!

00:08:56.680 --> 00:08:58.680
Kiso Market

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:07.290
What are we doing for lunch?
There are restaurants here.

00:09:09.170 --> 00:09:11.590
I don't want to squander any money.

00:09:14.840 --> 00:09:19.140
Huh? Are you thinking of
cooking the rice <i>now</i>?

00:09:19.140 --> 00:09:20.560
Excuse me...

00:09:23.480 --> 00:09:27.230
Please allow me to take care of lunch.

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:42.740
Thank you for waiting.

00:09:42.740 --> 00:09:43.950
Ooh!

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:48.540
I topped it with cream cheese and
the Kiso smoked salmon I just bought.

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:50.920
Please, have a taste.

00:09:54.590 --> 00:09:58.720
Mm-hmm, delicious.

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:02.260
Yum! I feel like a German
or Russian soldier!

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:05.560
Now if we had some peas and bacon,
it would be perfect.

00:10:05.560 --> 00:10:07.560
Glad to hear it.

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:56.110
{=1}Welcome to Higashiomi City, Shiga Prefecture

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:56.110
{=0}Roadside Station 5.1km ahead

00:11:05.870 --> 00:11:07.910
There's Lake Biwa!

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:13.960
Business Hotel Biwako Inn

00:11:31.850 --> 00:11:34.860
Oh, is supper ready? Let's eat!

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:38.400
You're getting the floor wet.
Go towel off and put some clothes on.

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:42.700
Aw, but curry is supposed
to be eaten naked.

00:11:55.040 --> 00:12:00.010
I hear that during the summer, they hold
a meeting of Cub owners in this park.

00:12:00.010 --> 00:12:01.340
Meeting?

00:12:01.340 --> 00:12:04.140
Over 400 different Cubs come together.

00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:06.890
There're lots of old ones
and unusual models, too.

00:12:06.890 --> 00:12:08.180
Oh, yeah?

00:12:08.180 --> 00:12:12.310
As a Cub rider, I've always wanted
to attend one of them.

00:12:12.310 --> 00:12:14.940
I'd like to go, too.

00:12:14.940 --> 00:12:16.480
Mm-hmm.

00:12:18.570 --> 00:12:22.150
I hope summer gets here soon.

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:13.210
The Sea of Japan doesn't seem
to have any surging waves, huh?

00:13:13.210 --> 00:13:14.370
That's too bad.

00:13:14.370 --> 00:13:16.170
Thank goodness.

00:13:16.170 --> 00:13:18.630
If Reiko saw any huge waves
coming in from the ocean,

00:13:18.630 --> 00:13:23.840
she'd be liable to sell her Hunter Cub
on the spot and buy a surfboard.

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:28.050
Huh? I was thinking <i>you'd</i>
be the one to do that.

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:32.430
Not a chance. I wouldn't
be able to get back home.

00:13:32.430 --> 00:13:34.810
Besides, compared to my Cub...

00:13:41.480 --> 00:13:43.570
I wonder how much I could get for it...

00:13:43.570 --> 00:13:44.860
Huh?!

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:52.060
Kyoto Prefecture

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:52.060
Maizuru City

00:13:58.850 --> 00:14:03.280
Hyogo Prefecture

00:14:27.610 --> 00:14:29.910
The Tottori Sand Dunes!

00:14:41.370 --> 00:14:44.320
Marine Products Direct Sales Center

00:14:58.750 --> 00:15:01.250
Guest 
House Mizuha

00:15:00.520 --> 00:15:02.520
Whoo, what a haul, what a haul!

00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:04.150
Ah, just a minute!

00:15:04.150 --> 00:15:05.900
Aww...

00:15:07.860 --> 00:15:10.110
Okay, say cheese!

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:18.730
Lake Shinji

00:15:33.010 --> 00:15:36.010
We're finally at the far end of Honshu.

00:15:36.010 --> 00:15:41.560
Amazing. Cubs really can go
anywhere in Japan, huh?

00:15:41.560 --> 00:15:43.560
Not just Japan, either.

00:15:47.360 --> 00:15:49.860
They can even go across the ocean.

00:16:14.620 --> 00:16:17.580
Net Café
Olive\h

00:16:27.440 --> 00:16:31.650
It looks like they're already starting
to bloom in Miyazaki and Kumamoto.

00:16:31.650 --> 00:16:34.740
We've already decided on our destination--

00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:38.660
the very farthest end of Japan
that our Cubs can take us.

00:16:38.660 --> 00:16:39.220
Mm-hmm.

00:16:39.220 --> 00:16:40.580
Right.

00:17:24.540 --> 00:17:26.210
We're here.

00:17:26.210 --> 00:17:27.710
Right.

00:17:27.710 --> 00:17:31.760
We've caught it--spring.

00:17:48.360 --> 00:17:50.900
When I said we should go
and see the cherry blossoms,

00:17:50.900 --> 00:17:54.280
I was sure that you were going
to say we couldn't do that.

00:17:55.240 --> 00:17:59.070
I was going to. But...

00:18:00.160 --> 00:18:04.410
Please save me again with your Super Cub.

00:18:06.040 --> 00:18:10.040
Please take this cold, dark winter...

00:18:10.040 --> 00:18:16.300
...and send it...
send it away somewhere...

00:18:19.300 --> 00:18:22.100
I'm begging you...

00:18:22.100 --> 00:18:24.350
I'm begging you...

00:18:25.310 --> 00:18:27.020
That's...

00:18:27.980 --> 00:18:31.820
...not something my Cub... can do.

00:18:37.530 --> 00:18:42.580
I thought we should try
and see if it actually could.

00:18:44.910 --> 00:18:47.540
It's really nice riding
with someone, isn't it?

00:18:47.540 --> 00:18:52.170
I always rode around by myself,
so this has been fun.

00:19:04.310 --> 00:19:07.350
Let's carry this back home with us.

00:19:07.350 --> 00:19:09.810
Back to our own town.

00:19:14.150 --> 00:19:20.990
By the day we returned,
our winterscape of a town had changed.

00:19:20.990 --> 00:19:24.950
The cherry blossoms had come out,
the sunlight shone down,

00:19:24.950 --> 00:19:28.790
and the hills and dales were
covered with fresh greenery.

00:19:28.790 --> 00:19:34.380
At last, spring was here.
No, we had brought spring home with us.

00:19:38.510 --> 00:19:41.130
It's completely spring here, too, huh?

00:19:58.780 --> 00:20:00.590
Eniwa Shii

00:20:02.070 --> 00:20:03.820
Hello.

00:20:05.080 --> 00:20:06.540
Huh?

00:20:12.080 --> 00:20:14.420
Is this Little Cub...?

00:20:14.420 --> 00:20:19.260
Well, um, I was going to talk
to both of you about this first,

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:23.470
but when we went to look at them,
they had this one, and I bought it!

00:20:23.470 --> 00:20:28.390
Ho... Brand new stock.
You must be loaded, huh?

00:20:28.390 --> 00:20:31.480
It was a marked-down, like-new bargain,

00:20:31.480 --> 00:20:34.610
so I got them to lower the price
and paid half of it myself.

00:20:34.610 --> 00:20:40.030
I borrowed the rest from Papa,
promising to pay him back by graduation.

00:20:40.030 --> 00:20:44.410
You can ride this and continue
your Italian café project, huh?

00:20:44.410 --> 00:20:45.620
Mm-hmm!

00:20:45.620 --> 00:20:50.250
With a Cub, I can go shopping anywhere.

00:20:50.250 --> 00:20:53.080
Riding a motorbike
in the spring feels good.

00:20:53.080 --> 00:20:55.460
That's why there are more
of them on the roads.

00:20:55.460 --> 00:20:57.090
You have to be careful.

00:20:57.090 --> 00:20:58.500
Then comes summer.

00:20:58.500 --> 00:21:01.380
It's not true what they say
about riding making it cooler,

00:21:01.380 --> 00:21:04.720
so if you're not careful,
you can get so hot you collapse.

00:21:04.720 --> 00:21:09.640
Then comes autumn, and winter again.
Winters are cold and long...

00:21:31.290 --> 00:21:35.540
I have no parents. No money, either.

00:21:35.540 --> 00:21:40.340
Nor do I have any hobbies, friends,
or goals for the future.

00:21:40.340 --> 00:21:45.470
But my days of nothingness
have changed just a little.

00:21:45.470 --> 00:21:49.050
Was it because I came across my Cub?

00:21:49.050 --> 00:21:50.850
No.

00:21:50.850 --> 00:21:54.560
If you sit back and do nothing,
a Cub won't help you.

00:21:54.560 --> 00:21:59.150
You probably have to have
a desire of your own.

00:21:59.150 --> 00:22:05.320
Like, say... wanting to turn at an unfamiliar
corner you've never turned at before.

00:22:05.320 --> 00:22:08.120
It doesn't have to be
any bigger than that.

00:22:08.120 --> 00:22:11.950
When you do, I'm sure
the Cub will respond.

00:22:13.580 --> 00:22:16.750
It isn't a magical, do-anything machine.

00:22:16.750 --> 00:22:22.670
But when you have to face a hurdle,
or come through with something...

00:22:22.670 --> 00:22:25.380
...it will definitely be there at your side.

00:22:26.430 --> 00:22:29.430
Such were our Super Cubs.

00:22:32.220 --> 00:22:36.100
I'm going to keep riding
forever... on my...

00:22:36.100 --> 00:22:38.020
...Super Cub.

00:22:36.100 --> 00:22:41.020
Episode 12

00:22:36.100 --> 00:22:41.020
Super Cub
